{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nTeams running several tracker projects against one codebase (or several repos against one ticket\nstore) cannot use the bridge: it is hard-wired to exactly one project at three points —\n`JiraConfig.project` is a single scalar (`_config_schema.py`), the inbound fetcher builds its JQL pair\nfrom one key and fails closed on an empty one (`fetcher.jqls_for`), and the applier aborts a pass when\nany outbound mutation targets a key outside that project (`applier.CrossProjectTargetError`). The only\nescape is the destructive one-way `scripts/retarget_jira_project.py`. Assignee preservation for\ntracker-unresolvable users is owned by in-progress bug `9b94-af9e-4acf-4dff` and taken as a dependency,\nnot duplicated here.\n\n(Full original description with line-anchored citations preserved verbatim as a ticket comment,\n2026-08-13.)\n\n## Approach\n\nModel many-to-many as one shared ticket store between N repos and N tracker projects. Each ticket\nrecords the project it syncs into and the repos it belongs to.\n\nThe STORE owns the project set — `.bridge_state/projects.json` on the tickets branch beside\n`bindings.json`/`prev_snapshot.json`. Reason (mechanical): `prev_snapshot.json` is last-known-remote\nstate; if two repos fetched different project subsets against one shared snapshot, each pass would\ndiff the other's projects as remote deletions. A store-owned project set removes that failure mode by\nconstruction and leaves no per-repo list to disagree.\n\nBuilt on the provider-neutral `bridge` verb group (epic `2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3`) and the backend-neutral\nport — `RemoteRef(vendor, instance, remote_id)`, `Backend.project` / `Backend.query_project`.\n`Backend.project` (\"the backend's effective write/create project scope\") is the per-repo default for\nrebar-created tickets; no new config key; generalizes beyond Jira.\n\nMigration writes NO events. The ticket project field is tri-state — absent=legacy, explicit-empty=\nnever sync, explicit key=sync there — mirroring `file_impact_scope` undeclared/none/paths\n(`docs/ticket-model.md`). Absent resolves against the legacy default recorded in the mapping, seeded by\nan idempotent check-then-act ensure unit (`docs/migrations.md`, the sanctioned seam; the ordered\nSchool-A ledger is explicitly not built). A per-ticket EDIT migration was rejected: four-figure event\nwrites under the store lock, and the MCP-boot entry runs the ensure sweep on a short lock budget and\nskips when contended — an event-writing migration would silently skip at one of its three entry points.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` — mapping store, fetch fan-out, outbound dispatch, cross-project guard.\n- `src/rebar/_store/ensures.py`, `_store/init.py` — the ensure unit seeding the mapping.\n- `src/rebar/_store/compat.py` — the conditional capability stamp.\n- `src/rebar/reducer/`, `schemas/ticket_state.schema.json`, `_commands/composer.py`, `_lib_writes.py`,\n  `_mcp_writes.py` — the two new ticket fields and their create-time arguments.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/` — the `bridge projects` subcommand.\n- `docs/` — the multi-project model, the mapping, and an ADR.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `bridge projects` lists, sets and removes project→repos entries on the store mapping, and the\n      same operations exist on the library and MCP surfaces; checked by a per-surface test asserting\n      each of the three surfaces reads back an entry written by another.\n- [ ] A store whose mapping holds two projects fetches both in a single pass and each ingested ticket\n      records the project it came from; checked by a reconciler test asserting one JQL pair AND one\n      enrichment pass (parent/comment/issuelink maps) is issued per configured project, with both\n      projects' enrichment data present in the merged snapshot, and asserting the recorded project\n      on each created ticket.\n- [ ] A ticket whose project is explicitly empty produces no outbound mutation; checked by an\n      outbound-differ test asserting an empty mutation list for that ticket while a sibling with a\n      project produces one.\n- [ ] A ticket created with an explicit project targets that project rather than the repo default;\n      checked by a dispatch test asserting the create call carries the ticket's project.\n- [ ] An outbound update targeting a project inside the configured set proceeds while one outside it\n      still raises `CrossProjectTargetError`; checked by a paired applier test covering both directions.\n- [ ] Every ticket in a pre-feature store resolves to the recorded legacy default with zero events\n      written; checked by a migration test asserting the store's event count is byte-identical before\n      and after the sweep and that each ticket resolves to the default.\n- [ ] A store whose mapping holds more than one project carries `multi-project-bridge` in\n      `.store-compat.json` `required_capabilities` and a binary lacking that capability refuses writes,\n      while a single-project store remains writable; checked by a store-compat test covering both.\n\n## Child decomposition (disjoint file sets; no edit conflicts)\n\n- **Project mapping store** — `.bridge_state/projects.json` + helpers + the ensure seed. Delivers migration/legacy-default criteria.\n- **`bridge projects` command surface** — subcommand + library/MCP parity per epic `2f79`. Delivers criterion 1.\n- **Ticket project field** — schema, CREATE data, reducer, create-time args on all three surfaces; promote-only rule (cannot change project of a bound ticket). Delivers empty-project criterion.\n- **Ticket repos field** — schema, reducer, create-time arg, inbound defaulting from the mapping.\n- **Multi-project inbound fetch** — fan-out + snapshot union; per-query truncation ceiling scoped per\n  project; the three per-project enrichment passes (`get_parent_map` / `get_comment_map` /\n  `get_issuelinks_map`) also fan across every configured project — one call per project, results\n  merged into the shared snapshot keyed by issue (single-project enrichment would silently drop\n  parent/comment/issuelink data for every project but one). Enrichment fidelity joins the\n  two-project fetch acceptance test. Delivers two-project fetch criterion.\n- **Multi-project outbound dispatch** — per-ticket project on create; guard relaxed from single project to set membership. Delivers explicit-project + guard criteria.\n- **Store-compat capability stamp** — conditional `required_capabilities` entry + fail-closed read. Delivers final criterion.\n- **Docs + ADR** — model, mapping, tri-state field, decision record.\n- **Live multi-project rehearsal** — LAST child: rehearse against two live Jira Cloud projects on an\n  isolated tickets-branch copy on the encrypted S3 remote (capability from epic `cf3c-1444-863e-49d7`,\n  hence the depends_on); dry-run-gated, all created issues removed. Fixtures cannot reach the\n  cross-project contamination failure mode this validates.\n- **Module-size relief** — several files this feature edits sit within ~30 lines of the 800 hard cap.\n  Behaviour-preserving extractions along existing seams, each ordered ahead of the story needing room;\n  they deliver no epic criterion (preconditions; their own criteria are unchanged suite + measured LOC).\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nAdditive at every layer. Absent project = legacy; a pre-feature store behaves as today, no operator\naction. A single-project store never receives the capability stamp, so older binaries keep working;\nonly a genuinely multi-project store fails closed on them — the intended protection (an older binary\nwould fetch its one project, see other projects' tickets as unbound, and create duplicates in the\nwrong project). Rollback is per-change on Gerrit; the mapping and capability entry are inert to older\nbinaries apart from the deliberate fail-closed, and deleting `.store-compat.json` returns every binary\nto implicit-legacy with the idempotent ensure re-stamping on the next covered write.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786610841368018001,"uuid":"4e0e7724-913d-418e-8783-e615f34afdb0"}